  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of China Food and Drug Administration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposed IDF project aims to assist China Food and Drug Administration (CFDA) to develop capacity to implement food safety regulation system by incorporating international best practices and adapting to the level of development. It is expected that the project will support CFDA to better understand and incorporate how other lead food regulatory agenceis deliver services, e.g., organization of food control, central register of food business organizations, risk assessment and risk management, use of international data and knowledge in food safety, the budget of inspection, number of inspectors, qualification and training of inspectors, and collobration among food safety institutions.  The proposed IDF project would support capacity building and technical assistance activities of CFDA newly created in 2013. CFDA is consolidating responsibilites of line ministries in charge of food safety and supervising food production from farm to folk to address overlapping, redundant, or missing food safety standards, and inconsistent interpretation and uneven application of food safety standards. This suppoprt would contribute to improving national food safety tools which are based on scientific knowledge and risk analysis, promoting coordination among food regulators and ensuring clear and consistent interpretation, and enforcement of food safety standards at national and local levels.</narrative>
  </description>
